act 19 LADDER COMMIT: the condition ladder L0-L5, stated before any census

The ordering obligation of the act 19 control plane requires the condition
ladder to be fixed by the control-plane blob and by nothing else, and stated
in the execution branch BEFORE any discriminating result enters it. This
commit is the record of that ordering, and it is record 2 of the five the
freeze requires.

verification/lean-mathlib/OIBridge/OrbitLawRigidity.lean carries the eight
budgeted definitions and nothing else:

  TransitionLaw        the transition family and the law it generates, whose
                       first conjunct is L4d, the descent to classes
  EvolvesTotally       L0
  PreservesAdmissible  L1
  Reversible           L3i and L3s, as two conjuncts, reported apart
  FactorizesOnProduct  L5
  LadderConds          the conjunction, carrying L2 and L4n inline
  LawEquiv             the law equivalence, which introduces no new
                       identification
  SameInitialOrbitPair the discriminating test, with the earlier-agreement
                       conjunct

NO DISCRIMINATING RESULT IS PRESENT AT THIS COMMIT. There is no proof of the
shared structural theorem, no census of the frozen candidate list, no
exhibited survivor, no exhibited failure of a rung, and no witness or
refutation of the discriminating test. The module contains no theorem at all:
every declaration is a definition, so the repository's no-unproved-declaration
rule and the freeze's ordering requirement do not collide.

The boundary is semantic and not proof-length based. Nothing here establishes,
by any proof however short, that a candidate satisfies or fails a rung.

Also: the module is imported by OIBridge.lean so continuous integration builds
it, and one census family entry is added for it.

